These scripts are all for maintaining the database. 

accessing the database: see wiki for how to set up 
https://trinity.physics.gatech.edu/internal/index.php?title=Database_for_collected_data

-------
userUpdateDatabase.py - This script creates all the .sql files using python. The script will prompt the user throughout to fill it in based on the wiki. The .sql files will be in the Output/ folder. This works on one night at a time.Nights with no data have a special NOData entry and should still have all the .sql's created. 


Lily: 

Nightly Classification runs as a cron job now and outputs yyyymmdd_AllFiles.txt nightly

if "attention needed" gets output, that means there's only one file for that night for some reason

userUpdateDatabase.py:
cd UpdateDB/
    outside container: 
        ./run_script_a.sh
    inside container: s_pygroup
        python3 userUpdateDatabase.py
input date, path, weather/data/ranking info
-> outputs weather, datainfo, celestial, ranking sqls to file_database/UpdateDB/Output/

To upload to database: TrinityLabComputer/Database/file_db/
    see file_db README


